PRACTICAL – 2
Title:

Security Testing of DIVA App using ADB

Aim:

To perform security testing of the DIVA Android application using Android Debug Bridge (ADB).

Objectives:
To understand the use of ADB in Android security testing
To install and configure ADB on Linux
To connect Android emulator/device using ADB
To analyze the DIVA application using ADB commands
To identify insecure configurations and vulnerabilities
Procedure:
(i) Install ADB

Open terminal and run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install adb -y

Verify installation:

adb version
(ii) Start Android Emulator
Open Android Studio
Launch Android Virtual Device (AVD)

Verify emulator connection:

adb devices

👉 Connected emulator/device will be displayed.

(iii) Download DIVA APK

Download APK:

wget https://github.com/0xArab/diva-apk-file/raw/main/DivaApplication.apk
(iv) Install DIVA APK
adb install DivaApplication.apk
(v) Open ADB Shell
adb shell
(vi) List Installed Packages
pm list packages

Find DIVA package:

pm list packages | grep diva
(vii) Access Application Information

Check package details:

dumpsys package jakhar.aseem.diva
(viii) Capture Application Logs
adb logcat

👉 Displays runtime logs generated by the application.

(ix) Pull Files from Device (Optional)
adb pull /sdcard/
Observation:
ADB connected successfully with Android emulator
DIVA APK was installed successfully
Installed packages and application details were retrieved
Runtime logs were captured using logcat
Application data and package information were analyzed successfully
Result:

Security testing of the DIVA application was successfully performed using ADB. Various ADB commands were used to analyze package information, logs, and application behavior on the Android emulator.

Viva Questions:
Q: What is ADB?

👉 Android Debug Bridge used for communication with Android devices/emulators.

Q: What is DIVA?

👉 Damn Insecure and Vulnerable App used for Android security testing.

Q: What does adb devices do?

👉 Displays connected Android devices or emulators.

Q: What is logcat?

👉 Tool used to capture Android system and application logs.

Important Commands
adb version
adb devices
adb install DivaApplication.apk
adb shell
adb logcat
